<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Valerius Triarius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Valerius Triarius was a Roman legate under Lucullus in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war">Third Mithridatic War</a>. In 67 BCE, while Lucullus was away, he attacked Mithridates VI near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zela">Zela</a> in Pontus and suffered a heavy defeat in which, according to ancient writers, thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and many officers died. The disaster allowed Mithridates to recover much of his kingdom.</p></div>
